d holds a large cash advantage, with $2.5 million banked to Flores's $0.7 million. Flores has still raised nearly $2.9 million, and national Republicans are investing attention, with JD Vance headlining a rally in the district.\n\nMost expert ratings call the race Lean Democratic, though Cook and Inside Elections rate it a Tossup, and prediction markets give Gonzalez roughly an 84% chance. The only recent independent poll shows Gonzalez up three. The forecast lands on a narrow Democratic lead with substantial uncertainty, appropriate for a district this marginal in a volatile midterm environment.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7969, "margin": 4.84}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7826, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7895, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8125, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7373, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7369, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7694, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7877, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7446, "margin": 4.0}]}